        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">If you can pay for it, the Body-Solid EXM2500S is the best home gym
            here</strong>, with a 210 lb stack and an in-home lifetime warranty; on a budget, the Marcy
            MWM-990 gives you a real 150 lb stack, and the Best Fitness BFMG20 does the same in a
            smaller room. Choose the BowFlex Xtreme 2 SE when weight and price matter more than
            stack feel, and the Total Gym EVOLVE when the ceiling or storage decides everything.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, read the resistance figure for what it is, measure the ceiling and
